= Fireblight Tree Care

Trees are sad, I don't want to move. Keep them alive

== Spray Care

- *#underline[Most important:]*
  - Spray right when buds show
  - Spray when leaves fall
  
- Can spray other times but its less benificial
- Spraying mid summer doesn't help much, just wastes product

- 1/2 gal more on trees (3.5 gal total, per tree)

- Ratios are ok, could increase pentra bark a bit, no concern for tree

- little droplets stick better

- can drip down tree, ok, but needs to stick

== Pruning

- Never cut! only prune in winter, colder the better

- Pole saw for tall branches

- tie back low branch until winter then cut it back to release weight

== 911

- if fireblight explodes, get injections, faster response than spraying, but more expensive (\~\$100 per tree)
